# Lesson 09 - BrowserManager

## Objective

Create a reusable component responsible for browser lifecycle management.

---

## Responsibilities

BrowserManager is responsible for:

- Starting Playwright
- Launching Chromium
- Creating Browser Contexts
- Creating Pages
- Closing browser resources

It does not know anything about LinkedIn or any other website.

---

## Lifecycle

BrowserManager

↓

start()

↓

new_page()

↓

stop()

---

## Why separate BrowserManager?

Many future publishers will reuse the same browser infrastructure.

Examples:

- LinkedInPublisher
- TeamsPublisher
- GitHubPublisher
- JiraPublisher

Keeping browser management separate avoids duplicated code and follows the Single Responsibility Principle.

---

## Key Takeaway

BrowserManager manages browsers.

Publishers manage websites.